=== ''Legion'' (2017–2019) ===
{{Main|Legion (TV series)|l1=''Legion'' (TV series)}}
[[File:Dan Stevens (46801499514).jpg|thumb|upright|Dan Stevens in 2019]]

Following the premiere of [[FX (TV channel)|FX]]'s ''[[Fargo (TV series)|Fargo]]'' in 2014, [[Noah Hawley]] deliberated ideas on an X-Men TV adaptation with FX producers.<ref name="HawleyHF">{{Cite web |last=Sepinwell |first=Alan |date=June 1, 2016 |title={{'}}''Fargo''{{'}} boss on Ewan McGregor in season 3, {{'}}''X-Men''{{'}} spin-off {{'}}''Legion'',' and his new hit novel |url=http://www.hitfix.com/whats-alan-watching/fargo-boss-on-ewan-mcgregor-in-season-3-x-men-spin-off-legion-and-his-new-hit-novel |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161023164324/http://www.hitfix.com/whats-alan-watching/fargo-boss-on-ewan-mcgregor-in-season-3-x-men-spin-off-legion-and-his-new-hit-novel |archive-date=October 23, 2016 |access-date=October 11, 2016 |work=[[HitFix]]}}</ref> Two concepts were pitched that Hawley rejected, including a show based on the [[Hellfire Club (comics)|Hellfire Club]].<ref name="HawleyHF" /><ref name="DonnerJan2017">{{Cite web |last=Schwartz |first=Terri |date=January 16, 2017 |title=''Legion'': ''X-Men'' Producer on How Professor X Fits in and Future TV Plans |url=https://ign.com/articles/2017/01/16/legion-x-men-producer-on-how-xavier-fits-in-and-future-tv-plans |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170116232827/http://www.ign.com/articles/2017/01/16/legion-x-men-producer-on-how-xavier-fits-in-and-future-tv-plans |archive-date=January 16, 2017 |access-date=January 17, 2017 |publisher=[[IGN]]}}</ref> Afterwards, he turned to Kinberg for guidance and the two discussed [[Legion (Marvel Comics)|David Haller]], the son of Xavier with [[schizophrenia]] whose hallucinations are an expression of a superpower.<ref name="HawleyHF" /><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Halloway |first=Daniel |date=January 24, 2017 |title='Legion': Creator Noah Hawley on Taking FX Series Beyond X-Men |url=https://variety.com/2017/tv/news/legion-noah-hawley-fx-dan-stevens-1201967490/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240308150612/https://variety.com/2017/tv/news/legion-noah-hawley-fx-dan-stevens-1201967490/ |archive-date=March 8, 2024 |access-date=March 5, 2026 |magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> Hawley said he found this quality fascinating and sought to convey the story using Haller's condition to play on perspective.<ref name="HawleyHF" /> ''Legion'' is situated in a timeline tangential to the ''X-Men'' films.<ref name="LandgrafJan2016">{{Cite web |last=Schwartz |first=Terri |date=January 16, 2016 |title=FX'S ''Legion'' Anticipated to Debut in 2016; Series Not Set in X-Men Film Universe |url=https://ign.com/articles/2016/01/16/fxs-legion-anticipated-for-2016-tv-season |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160116195501/http://www.ign.com/articles/2016/01/16/fxs-legion-anticipated-for-2016-tv-season |archive-date=January 16, 2016 |access-date=October 11, 2016 |publisher=[[IGN]]}}</ref><ref name="SingerAug2016">{{Cite web |last=Szalai |first=Georg |date=August 25, 2016 |title=Bryan Singer, Peter Rice Talk FX's {{'}}''Legion'',' Start of {{'}}''X-Men''{{'}} Movie Franchise |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/bryan-singer-peter-rice-edinburgh-922716 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161011193830/http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/bryan-singer-peter-rice-edinburgh-922716 |archive-date=October 11, 2016 |access-date=October 11, 2016 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref><ref name="NYCC2016">{{Cite web |last=Wigler |first=Josh |date=October 9, 2016 |title={{'}}''Legion''{{'}} Premiere Previewed at NYCC: A Look Inside FX's Upcoming {{'}}''X-Men''{{'}} Series |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/legion-premiere-previewed-at-nycc-936647 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161010183614/http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/legion-premiere-previewed-at-nycc-936647 |archive-date=October 10, 2016 |access-date=October 11, 2016 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref>

''Legion'' consists of 27 episodes split between three seasons, broadcast from 2017 to 2019.<ref name="legion3">{{Cite web |last=Robinson |first=Joanna |date=June 24, 2019 |title=How Legion Creator Noah Hawley Got the Show Back on Track in Season Three |url=https://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2019/06/legion-season-3-interview-noah-hawley |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221001111412/https://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2019/06/legion-season-3-interview-noah-hawley |archive-date=October 1, 2022 |access-date=March 5, 2026 |website=[[Vanity Fair (magazine)|Vanity Fair]] |url-access=subscription}}</ref> The show's first season sees Haller honing his newfound powers after Sydney Barrett ([[Rachel Keller (actress)|Rachel Keller]]) convinces him that he is in fact lucid.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Tallerico |first=Brian |date=April 3, 2018 |title=Everything to Remember About Legion Before Watching Season Two |url=https://www.vulture.com/2018/04/legion-what-happened-in-season-1.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240126061920/https://www.vulture.com/2018/04/legion-what-happened-in-season-1.html |archive-date=January 26, 2024 |access-date=March 5, 2026 |website=[[Vulture (website)|Vulture]]}}</ref> In season two, Haller embarks on a quest to vanquish [[Shadow King|Amahl Farouk / Shadow King]] ([[Navid Negahban]]) with a government agency of mutants known as Division Three, culminating in him sexually assaulting Barrett.<ref name="legion3" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=Haigis |first=Michael |date=April 3, 2018 |title=Review: 'Legion: Season Two' |url=https://www.slantmagazine.com/tv/legion-season-two/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230424231659/https://www.slantmagazine.com/tv/legion-season-two/ |archive-date=April 24, 2023 |access-date=March 5, 2026 |website=[[Slant Magazine]]}}</ref> He becomes a hippie cult leader in hiding in the show's final season, seeking to exploit the time traveling abilities of a mutant named Switch ([[Lauren Tsai]]) to undo his misdeeds.<ref name="legion3" /><ref>{{Cite news |last=Traver |first=Ben |date=June 24, 2019 |title='Legion' Review: Season 3 Takes an Exciting Approach to Time Travel, Even If It Gets a Bit Lost |url=https://www.indiewire.com/criticism/shows/legion-season-3-review-fx-tv-show-1202151743/ |access-date=March 5, 2026 |work=[[Indiewire]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250528223525/https://www.indiewire.com/criticism/shows/legion-season-3-review-fx-tv-show-1202151743/ |archive-date=May 28, 2025 |url-status=live |language=en-US}}</ref> [[Dan Stevens]] portrays Haller, leading a starring cast featuring Keller, [[Aubrey Plaza]], [[Jean Smart]], [[Jeremie Harris]], [[Amber Midthunder]], [[Katie Aselton]], [[Bill Irwin]], [[Jemaine Clement]], and [[Hamish Linklater]].<ref name="SeriesOrder">{{Cite web |date=May 31, 2016 |title=FX Networks Picks Up {{'}}''Legion''{{'}} to Series |url=http://marvel.com/news/tv/26239/fx_networks_picks_up_legion_to_series |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160610071525/http://marvel.com/news/tv/26239/fx_networks_picks_up_legion_to_series |archive-date=June 10, 2016 |access-date=October 11, 2016 |publisher=[[Marvel Entertainment]]}}</ref><ref name="MainCast">{{Cite web |date=February 4, 2016 |title=Dan Stevens, Aubrey Plaza & Jean Smart Cast in FX Networks' Pilot for {{'}}''Legion''{{'}} |url=http://marvel.com/news/tv/25702/dan_stevens_aubrey_plaza_jean_smart_cast_in_fx_networks_pilot_for_legion |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160329220844/http://marvel.com/news/tv/25702/dan_stevens_aubrey_plaza_jean_smart_cast_in_fx_networks_pilot_for_legion |archive-date=March 29, 2016 |access-date=October 11, 2016 |publisher=[[Marvel Entertainment]]}}</ref> Negahban was promoted to the main cast in season two, likewise Tsai for season three.<ref name="Negahban">{{Cite web |last=Nemetz |first=Dave |date=January 5, 2018 |title=''Legion'' Adds Homeland Alum Navid Negahban in Season 2 Villain Recast |url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/legion-season-2-cast-navid-negahban-ahmal-farouk-shadow-king-901991/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180117043725/http://tvline.com/2018/01/05/legion-season-2-cast-navid-negahban-ahmal-farouk-shadow-king/ |archive-date=January 17, 2018 |access-date=January 5, 2018 |publisher=[[TVLine]]}}</ref><ref name="TsaiSwitch">{{Cite web |last=Otterson |first=Joe |date=January 9, 2019 |title={{'}}''Legion''{{'}} Season 3 Casts Lauren Tsai (EXCLUSIVE) |url=https://variety.com/2019/tv/news/legion-season-3-lauren-tsai-1203103398/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190110183502/https://variety.com/2019/tv/news/legion-season-3-lauren-tsai-1203103398/ |archive-date=January 10, 2019 |access-date=January 10, 2019 |website=Variety}}</ref> Among the actors employed in recurring roles were [[Harry Lloyd]], [[Stephanie Corneliussen]], and [[Jon Hamm]].<ref name="X">{{Cite web |last=Butler |first=Mary Anne |date=February 4, 2019 |title={{'}}''Legion''{{'}} Adds Professor X to Their Season 3 Cast |url=https://www.bleedingcool.com/2019/02/04/legion-adds-professor-x-to-their-season-3-cast/ |access-date=February 4, 2019 |website=[[Bleeding Cool News]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Wigler |first=Josh |date=April 3, 2018 |title='Legion' Creator Reveals the 'Mad' Backstory to Season 2's New Narrator |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/legion-season-2-jon-hamm-is-narrator-1099475/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250804212053/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/legion-season-2-jon-hamm-is-narrator-1099475/ |archive-date=August 4, 2025 |access-date=March 5, 2026 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref>

=== ''The Gifted'' (2017–2019) ===
{{Main|The Gifted (American TV series)|l1=''The Gifted'' (American TV series)}}

Around the same time, ''The Gifted'', an X-Men series about a family fleeing state persecution after the parents discover their children have mutant powers,<ref name="PutPilot">{{Cite web |last=Wagmeister |first=Elizabeth |date=July 12, 2016 |title=Marvel {{'}}''X-Men''{{'}} Series from Matt Nix, Bryan Singer Lands Put Pilot Commitment at Fox (EXCLUSIVE) |url=https://variety.com/2016/tv/news/marvel-fox-series-matt-nix-pilot-commmitment-1201812851/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170126141222/http://variety.com/2016/tv/news/marvel-fox-series-matt-nix-pilot-commmitment-1201812851/ |archive-date=January 26, 2017 |access-date=January 20, 2017 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref><ref name="PilotOrderb">{{Cite web |last=Ge |first=Linda |date=January 24, 2017 |title=Matt Nix's ''X-Men'' Drama Ordered to Pilot at Fox |url=https://www.thewrap.com/matt-nixs-x-men-drama-ordered-to-pilot-at-fox/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170124231628/http://www.thewrap.com/matt-nixs-x-men-drama-ordered-to-pilot-at-fox/ |archive-date=January 24, 2017 |access-date=January 25, 2017 |website=[[TheWrap]]}}</ref> ran on [[Fox Broadcasting Company|Fox]] for two seasons.<ref name="tgcancelled1">{{Cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=April 17, 2019 |title='The Gifted' Canceled By Fox After 2 Seasons; Marvel Drama Could Potentially Find New Home At Disney |url=https://deadline.com/2019/04/the-gifted-canceled-fox-2-seasons-marvel-drama-new-home-disney-1202598063/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260217193209/https://deadline.com/2019/04/the-gifted-canceled-fox-2-seasons-marvel-drama-new-home-disney-1202598063/ |archive-date=February 17, 2026 |access-date=March 5, 2026 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> A [[20th Television]] and [[Marvel Television]] co-production, the show was conceived by [[Matt Nix]]; he pitched ''The Gifted'' as "''[[Running on Empty (1988 film)|Running on Empty]]'' with mutants".<ref name="PutPilot" /><ref name="RunningEmpty">{{Cite web |last=Radish |first=Christina |date=October 2, 2017 |title={{'}}''The Gifted''{{'}} Showrunner Matt Nix on Why the Show Is 'Running on Empty' with Mutants |url=https://collider.com/the-gifted-matt-nix-interview/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171004222444/http://collider.com/the-gifted-matt-nix-interview |archive-date=October 4, 2017 |access-date=October 4, 2017 |website=[[Collider (website)|Collider]]}}</ref> Nix chose an ordinary family as the central focus believing it was more appropriate for television than conventional superheroes.<ref name="EWPitch">{{Cite magazine |last=Li |first=Shirley |date=September 20, 2017 |title=''The Gifted'': Showrunner talks pressure of building an ''X-Men'' series with mass appeal |url=https://ew.com/tv/2017/09/20/the-gifted-matt-nix-pressure-marvel-fox/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171005000325/http://ew.com/tv/2017/09/20/the-gifted-matt-nix-pressure-marvel-fox/ |archive-date=October 5, 2017 |access-date=October 5, 2017 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref> A cast of nine actors received top billing: [[Stephen Moyer]], [[Amy Acker]], [[Sean Teale]], [[Natalie Alyn Lind]], [[Percy Hynes White]], [[Jamie Chung]], [[Coby Bell]], [[Blair Redford]], and [[Emma Dumont]].<ref name="SeriesOrderb">{{Cite web |last=Wagmeister |first=Elizabeth |date=May 9, 2017 |title=Fox Greenlights Marvel Action Series {{'}}''The Gifted''{{'}} From Bryan Singer & Matt Nix – Watch First Teaser |url=https://variety.com/2017/tv/news/fox-marvel-series-bryan-singer-watch-teaser-1202421542/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170510021104/http://variety.com/2017/tv/news/fox-marvel-series-bryan-singer-watch-teaser-1202421542/ |archive-date=May 10, 2017 |access-date=May 10, 2017 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> ''The Gifted'', like ''Legion'', inhabits the same fictional universe as the ''X-Men'' films in a separate timeline.<ref name="DonnerJan2017" /><ref name="NixColliderJan2017">{{cite web |url=https://collider.com/x-men-series-fox/#images |title=Fox's Upcoming X-Men Series Will Connect to the Movie Universe, Features New Characters |last=Keene |first=Allison |work=[[Collider (website)|Collider]] |date=January 11, 2017 |access-date=March 6, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170119090253/http://collider.com/x-men-series-fox/ |archive-date=January 19, 2017 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="SDCC17">{{cite web |url=http://www.cbr.com/the-gifted-panel-fox-marvel-sdcc-2017/ |title=SDCC: Fox's The Gifted Panel |last=Ching |first=Albert |work=[[Comic Book Resources]] |date=July 21, 2017 |access-date=March 6, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170722071749/http://www.cbr.com/the-gifted-panel-fox-marvel-sdcc-2017/ |archive-date=July 22, 2017 |url-status=live}}</ref>

The show's 13-episode first season debuted on October 2, 2017.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.avclub.com/a-two-hour-season-finale-finds-the-gifted-at-a-crossroa-1822093914 |title=A two-hour season finale finds The Gifted at a crossroads where its best meets its worst |last=Hassenger |first=Jessie |website=[[The A.V. Club]] |date=January 16, 2018 |access-date=March 6, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913175044/https://www.avclub.com/a-two-hour-season-finale-finds-the-gifted-at-a-crossroa-1822093914 |archive-date=September 13, 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://deadline.com/2017/06/fox-fall-2017-premiere-dates-empire-marvel-the-gifted-seth-macfarlane-orville-1202118456/ |title=Fox Sets Fall 2017 Premiere Dates: 'Empire', New Marvel Drama 'The Gifted', Seth MacFarlane's 'Orville' & More |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |date=June 22, 2017 |access-date=March 6, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170622193900/http://deadline.com/2017/06/fox-fall-2017-premiere-dates-empire-marvel-the-gifted-seth-macfarlane-orville-1202118456/ |archive-date=June 22, 2017 |url-status=live}}</ref> In January 2018, Fox renewed ''The Gifted'' for a second season, which aired to significantly lower ratings than season one.<ref name="tgcancelled1" /><ref name="Season2">{{Cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=January 4, 2018 |title={{'}}''The Gifted''{{'}} Renewed For Season 2 By Fox – TCA |url=https://deadline.com/2018/01/the-gifted-renewed-season-2-fox-1202235489/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180119103317/http://deadline.com/2018/01/the-gifted-renewed-season-2-fox-1202235489/ |archive-date=January 19, 2018 |access-date=January 4, 2018 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> The series was cancelled in April 2019.<ref name="Cancellation">{{Cite web |last=Goldberg |first=Lesley |date=April 17, 2019 |title='The Gifted,' 'Rel' Canceled at Fox |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/gifted-rel-canceled-at-fox-1202943 |access-date=April 17, 2019 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref>

== Cancellation ==
Fox began merger talks with Disney in late 2017.<ref name="merger1">{{Cite news |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2017/11/06/21st-century-fox-has-been-holding-talks-to-sell-most-of-company-to-disney-sources.html |title=21st Century Fox has been holding talks to sell most of the company to Disney: Sources |last=Faber |first=David |date=November 6, 2017 |publisher=[[CNBC]] |access-date=March 3, 2026 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180706021750/https://www.cnbc.com/2017/11/06/21st-century-fox-has-been-holding-talks-to-sell-most-of-company-to-disney-sources.html |archive-date=July 6, 2018}}</ref> Executives discussed an acquisition amid the launch of Disney's streaming service, [[Disney+]], and believed such would enhance its competitiveness.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2019/04/12/disney-wouldnt-have-bought-fox-assets-without-streaming-plans-iger-says.html |title=Iger says Disney bought Fox because of value it adds to streaming service: 'The light bulb went off' |last=Franck |first=Thomas |date=April 12, 2019 |publisher=[[CNBC]] |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190412184259/https://www.cnbc.com/2019/04/12/disney-wouldnt-have-bought-fox-assets-without-streaming-plans-iger-says.html |archive-date=April 12, 2019 |access-date=March 3, 2026}}</ref> This resulted in a brief bidding war with [[Comcast Corporation]] in June 2018, ending when Disney increased its offer to $71.3 billion.<ref name="disneycloses" /><ref>{{Cite web |date=March 19, 2019 |title=Comcast Ends Pursuit of Fox, Bidding War With Disney |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/general-news/comcast-ends-pursuit-fox-bidding-war-disney-1127251/ |first=Georg |last=Szalai |access-date=March 3, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250225120546/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/general-news/comcast-ends-pursuit-fox-bidding-war-disney-1127251/ |archive-date=February 25, 2025 |url-status=live |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> The acquisition was finalized on March 20, 2019,<ref name="disneycloses">{{Cite web |date=March 19, 2019 |title=Disney Closes $71.3{{nbsp}}Billion Fox Deal, Creating Global Content Powerhouse |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/disney-closes-fox-deal-creating-global-content-powerhouse-1174498 |first1=Georg |last1=Szalai |first2=Paul |last2=Bond |access-date=March 20, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260227164006/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/general-news/disney-closes-fox-deal-creating-global-content-powerhouse-1174498/ |archive-date=February 27, 2026 |url-status=live |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> which transferred the film rights to the X-Men and associated characters to Disney and subsidiary [[Marvel Studios]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=March 27, 2019 |title=Marvel just got back together with the X-Men. But it's complicated. |url=https://www.vox.com/culture/2019/3/27/18280941/marvel-fox-disney-merger-x-men |first=Alex |last=Abad-Santos |access-date=March 3, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260210120928/https://www.vox.com/culture/2019/3/27/18280941/marvel-fox-disney-merger-x-men |archive-date=February 10, 2026 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |website=[[Vox (website)|Vox]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=February 18, 2023 |title=Disney got 'The Simpsons' and 'Avatar.' But some now see the Fox deal as a mistake |url=https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/business/story/2023-02-18/disney-fox-purchase-iger-murdoch-analysis |first=Meg |last=James |access-date=March 3, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260116193743/https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/business/story/2023-02-18/disney-fox-purchase-iger-murdoch-analysis |archive-date=January 16, 2026 |url-status=live |website=[[Los Angeles Times]]}}</ref> Thus, [[List of unproduced X-Men film series projects|all planned adaptations from Fox were effectively cancelled]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=March 20, 2019 |title=The X-Men Projects That Likely Won't Be Made at Disney |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/lost-x-men-movies-arent-joining-marvel-universe-1195993/ |first=Graeme |last=McMillan |access-date=March 3, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241217000522/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/lost-x-men-movies-arent-joining-marvel-universe-1195993/ |archive-date=December 17, 2024 |url-status=live |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref><ref name="mcu1">{{Cite web |date=April 3, 2019 |title=New 'Avengers: Endgame' Footage Hits CinemaCon |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/new-avengers-endgame-scene-shows-captain-marvel-joining-team-1199385/ |first1=Carolyn |last1=Giardina |first2=Pamela |last2=McClintock |access-date=March 3, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230713044836/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/new-avengers-endgame-scene-shows-captain-marvel-joining-team-1199385/ |archive-date=July 13, 2023 |url-status=live |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> X-Men films under Disney ownership will be released as part of the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] (MCU).<ref name="mcu1" /> Numerous cast members from Fox's ''X-Men'' films have reprised their roles in MCU productions that are part of its [[Multiverse Saga]], ahead of the introduction of a rebooted X-Men cast for the MCU's [[X-Men (2028 film)|untitled ''X-Men'' film]] (2028).<ref>{{Cite web |last=Moreau |first=Jordan |date=2026-08-15 |title=‘X-Men’ Movie Casts Inde Navarrette as Rogue, Christopher Abbott as Prof. X, Adam Driver as Mr. Sinister and Maya Boyd as Storm |url=https://variety.com/2026/film/news/x-men-cast-inde-navarrette-rogue-christopher-abbott-prof-x-adam-driver-mr-sinister-1236817698/ |access-date=2026-09-29 |website=Variety |language=en-US}}</ref>

== Timeline ==

Events in the main continuity ''X-Men'' films are traditionally placed in two timelines.<ref name="filmcontinuity" /> The original timeline starts with ''X-Men Origins: Wolverine'', continuing through ''X-Men: First Class'', ''X-Men'', ''X2'', ''X-Men: The Last Stand'', ''The Wolverine'', and up to ''X-Men: Days of Future Past''.<ref name="gizmodotimeline">{{Cite magazine |last=Whitbrook |first=James |date=June 18, 2019 |title=A Crazed Attempt to Discern the X-Men Movie Timeline in Its Entirety After Dark Phoenix |url=https://gizmodo.com/a-crazed-attempt-to-discern-the-x-men-movie-timeline-in-1835423981 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250622152651/https://gizmodo.com/a-crazed-attempt-to-discern-the-x-men-movie-timeline-in-1835423981 |archive-date=June 22, 2025 |access-date=March 10, 2026 |magazine=[[Gizmodo]]}}</ref> The settings are mostly contemporaneous save for ''X-Men Origins: Wolverine'' (set between 1845 and 1979), ''X-Men: First Class'' (1962), and ''X-Men: Days of Future Past'' (partially 2023).<ref name="gizmodotimeline" /><ref name="timecontinuity">{{Cite magazine |last=Dockterman |first=Eliana |date=April 27, 2022 |title=A Guide to All the Major Cinematic Multiverses |url=https://time.com/6169255/cinematic-multiverse-list/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250217211458/https://time.com/6169255/cinematic-multiverse-list/ |archive-date=February 17, 2025 |access-date=March 10, 2026 |magazine=[[Time (magazine)|Time]]}}</ref> From ''X-Men: Days of Future Past'', a new timeline emerges when Wolverine is sent on a mission to prevent the assassination of Bolivar Trask in 1973, which [[retcon|retroactively alters]] all established film continuity.<ref name="filmcontinuity" /><ref name="slashfilmtimeline" /><ref name="slashfilmtimeline2">{{Cite magazine |last=Evangelista |first=Chris |date=June 15, 2019 |title='Dark Phoenix' Director Simon Kinberg Attempts To Make Sense Of The Nonsensical 'X-Men' Timeline |url=https://www.slashfilm.com/567098/x-men-timeline-explained/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250825031703/https://www.slashfilm.com/567098/x-men-timeline-explained/ |archive-date=August 25, 2025 |access-date=March 10, 2026 |magazine=[[SlashFilm|/Film]]}}</ref> This second timeline includes ''X-Men: Apocalypse'' and ''Dark Phoenix'', spanning from 1983 to 1992.<ref name="gizmodotimeline" /><ref name="slashfilmtimeline">{{Cite magazine |last=Garza |first=Joe |date=January 15, 2023 |title=The X-Men Timeline Explained |url=https://www.slashfilm.com/1167994/the-x-men-timeline-explained/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250902220654/https://www.slashfilm.com/1167994/the-x-men-timeline-explained/ |archive-date=September 2, 2025 |access-date=March 10, 2026 |magazine=[[SlashFilm|/Film]]}}</ref>

However, continuity in the films is not uniform and has been subjected to perceived errors related to storytelling and characters.{{efn|Attributed to multiple sources:<ref name="darkphoenix1" /><ref name="filmcontinuity" /><ref name="esquirecontinuity">{{Cite magazine |last=Nero |first=Dom |date=June 6, 2019 |title=An Exhaustive Explainer of X-Men's Deeply Confusing Timeline |url=https://www.esquire.com/entertainment/movies/a27758267/x-men-timeline-explained/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250817205634/https://www.esquire.com/entertainment/movies/a27758267/x-men-timeline-explained/ |archive-date=August 17, 2025 |access-date=March 13, 2026 |magazine=[[Esquire (magazine)|Esquire]]}}</ref><ref name="denofgeekcontinuity">{{Cite magazine |last=Burt |first=Kayti |date=June 5, 2019 |title=Explaining the X-Men Movie Timelines |url=https://www.denofgeek.com/movies/explaining-the-x-men-movie-timelines/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251116070456/https://www.denofgeek.com/movies/explaining-the-x-men-movie-timelines/ |archive-date=November 16, 2025 |access-date=March 13, 2026 |magazine=[[Den of Geek]]}}</ref><ref name="thrcontinuity">{{Cite magazine |last=Newby |first=Richard |date=July 26, 2024 |title=All the X-Men Franchise Movies, Ranked |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/lists/best-x-men-movies/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260225094525/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/lists/best-x-men-movies/ |archive-date=February 25, 2026 |access-date=March 13, 2026 |magazine=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref><ref name="vulturecontinuity">{{Cite magazine |last=Adlakha |first=Siddhant |date=July 26, 2024 |title=There's a Big Ol' Timeline Discrepancy in Deadpool & Wolverine |url=https://www.vulture.com/article/the-big-ol-timeline-retcon-of-deadpool-and-wolverine.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260129090407/https://www.vulture.com/article/the-big-ol-timeline-retcon-of-deadpool-and-wolverine.html |archive-date=January 29, 2026 |access-date=March 13, 2026 |magazine=[[Vulture (website)|Vulture]]}}</ref>}} The ''Deadpool'' films, for example, feature a distinct interpretation of Deadpool than ''X-Men Origins: Wolverine'' despite being played by the same actor,{{sfn|Taylor|2024}} though cameos from the young X-Men in ''Deadpool 2'' attempt to convey these films are also part of the new timeline.<ref name="denofgeekcontinuity2">{{Cite magazine |last=Crow |first=David |date=May 20, 2018 |title=Deadpool 2 Makes the X-Men Movies Timeline More Confusing! |url=https://www.denofgeek.com/movies/deadpool-2-x-men-movies-timeline-confusing/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260112211741/https://www.denofgeek.com/movies/deadpool-2-x-men-movies-timeline-confusing/ |archive-date=January 12, 2026 |access-date=March 13, 2026 |magazine=[[Den of Geek]]}}</ref> Jackman stated that ''Logan'' transpires in an alternate timeline, contradicting Mangold's claim that it does in fact occur in tandem with the core films.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Schmidt |first=Joe |date=January 21, 2017 |title=Hugh Jackman Says Logan is Set in Different Universe from X-Men Films |url=https://comicbook.com/marvel/news/hugh-jackman-logan-wolverine-alternate-universe-x-men/ |work=[[ComicBook.com]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260210143104/https://comicbook.com/marvel/news/hugh-jackman-logan-wolverine-alternate-universe-x-men/ |archive-date=February 10, 2026 |url-status=live |access-date=March 13, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Colbert |first=Stephen M. |date=January 23, 2017 |title=Logan Director Clarifies Hugh Jackman's 'Different Universe' Statement |url=https://screenrant.com/logan-movie-director-x-men-movies-universe-connections/ |work=[[Screen Rant]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260212154420/https://screenrant.com/logan-movie-director-x-men-movies-universe-connections/ |archive-date=February 12, 2026 |url-status=live |access-date=March 13, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Melrose |first=Kevin |date=2017-01-23 |title=Logan Director Clarifies Film's Place in X-Men Continuity |url=https://www.cbr.com/logan-x-men-continuity/ |access-date=2026-06-06 |website=CBR |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Dyce |first=Andrew |date=2017-03-05 |title=When is Logan in The X-Men Movie Timeline? |url=https://screenrant.com/logan-movie-xmen-future-year/ |access-date=2026-06-06 |website=ScreenRant |language=en}}</ref> ''The New Mutants'' contains some references to the X-Men though bears no obvious relationship to events in the main continuity films.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bell |first=Josh |date=August 27, 2025 |title=The Worst Marvel Mutant Movie Doesn't Deserve Its Dire Reputation |url=https://www.inverse.com/entertainment/the-new-mutants-5-year-anniversary |access-date=March 13, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260120121624/https://www.inverse.com/entertainment/the-new-mutants-5-year-anniversary |archive-date=January 20, 2026 |url-status=live |website=[[Inverse (website)|Inverse]]}}</ref> Nevertheless, Marvel designated the ''X-Men'' universe as [[Earth-10005]] within the context of their [[Multiverse (Marvel Comics)|multiverse]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Johnston |first=Dais |date=July 26, 2024 |title=Deadpool & Wolverine Just Sneakily Confirmed a Weird Piece of MCU Canon |url=https://www.inverse.com/entertainment/deadpool-and-wolverine-earth-10005-x-men-explained |access-date=March 9, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260121105037/https://www.inverse.com/entertainment/deadpool-and-wolverine-earth-10005-x-men-explained |archive-date=January 21, 2026 |url-status=live |website=[[Inverse (website)|Inverse]]}}</ref>
